/T (Text Field50)
/V (Environmental Monitoring \050EM\051 Recoveries Review\072\015 \015ISO 5 BSC and Personnel Evaluation\072\015Upon review of the environmental monitoring data\054 absence of microbial recovery \050No Growth\051 was demonstrated across all critical ISO 5 zones and personnel monitoring on the date of testing\056 Daily personnel monitoring for processing analyst Ellen Bennett and changeover analyst Karla Silva yielded no microbial growth on left and right fingertip touch plates\056 Daily surface sampling \0504 locations\051 and settling plates within processing BSC E001938 and changeover BSC E001937 yielded no microbial growth\056\015 \015Cleanroom EM Evaluation\072\015Weekly surface monitoring of Cleanroom L\055Suite conducted on 01Oct26 demonstrated no microbial recovery across all sampled cleanroom surfaces\054 confirming effective sanitization and surface control\056\015 \015Weekly active air monitoring of Cleanroom L\055Suite conducted on 01Oct26 demonstrated no microbial recovery in ISO 7 cleanroom 145 and ISO 8 anteroom 143\073 however\054 1 CFU under test sample ETX\055261012\0550430 was recovered from ISO 7 cleanroom 144 Section II \050identified as Staphylococcus epidermidis\051\054 and 5 CFUs under test sample ETX\055261012\0550433 were recovered from outermost ISO 8 room 142 \050identified as Staphylococcus epidermidis\054 Pseudomonas parafulva\054 Bacillus safensis\054 Corynebacterium xerosis\054 and Corynebacterium ureicelerivorans\051\056 The recovered organisms are common environmental isolates with morphology distinctly different from the Cocci shaped morphology observed in the failing test sample\054 and no microbial match could be established\056\015 \015It is important to emphasize that all sample processing activities were performed strictly within the validated ISO 5 BSC E001938 and changeover activities within ISO 5 BSC E001937\054 both located in the ISO 7 cleanroom \050144\051\056 There is minimal exposure of the test sample to ambient ISO 8 air\054 as samples and supplies are transferred in disinfected\054 closed containers on carts through the layered cleanroom suites\056 Furthermore\054 the recoveries occurred in the general cleanroom and lower\055classified ISO 8 outer room environments\054 which are physically segregated from the ISO 5 processing zone by closed doors and an outward\055cascading positive air pressure gradient\056 In conjunction with the complete absence of microbial growth on all analyst glove touch plates\054 settling plates\054 and ISO 5 BSC work surfaces throughout testing\054 there is no plausible contamination transfer pathway from the ambient environment to the test sample\056\015 \015Monthly cleaning and disinfection of the cleanrooms \050ISO 7\051 and their containing biosafety cabinets \050ISO 5\051 were performed on 27Sep26 for L\055Suite\054 as per MICRO\055SOP\0559\054 Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology\056 It was documented that all chemical indicators passed\054 verifying that environmental sanitization remained validated and in control prior to testing\056\015 \015Analyzing a 6\055month sample history for Link Pharmacy \050E19112\051\054 this specific analyte \042Tirzepatide\057Levocarnitine 17mg\057100mg\057mL \0501ml\051\042 has had no prior Out\055of\055Specification \050OOS\051 occurrences under ScanRDI sterility testing\056\015 \015All samples processed on the same day were also evaluated for evidence of sample\055to\055sample cross\055contamination\056 The test sample ETX\055260929\0550931 was the 39th sample processed by Ellen Bennett during the 2nd Shift on 01Oct26 within BSC E001938 \050Cleanroom 144\054 L\055Suite\051\056 All other samples processed by Ellen Bennett during this shift yielded negative results\056 Review of laboratory records identified one other sample that yielded a positive result on 01Oct26\054 documented under OOS\055262285 for CasaPharma Rx \050E72585\051\054 sample ETX\055260930\0550635 \050Tirzepatide\057B12 15mg\0571mg\0570\0565mL \055 2mL\051\056 However\054 that sample was prepared by Pagan Gary and processed by America Alanis \05011th sample processed\051 during the 1st Shift in an entirely separate suite and biosafety cabinet \050BSC E001312\054 Parallel Suite\051\056 The two testing events were completely segregated by shift\054 processing analyst\054 prepping personnel\054 physical suite\054 and primary containment equipment\056 Furthermore\054 analyst Ellen Bennett verified that gloves were disinfected between samples and standard aseptic techniques were strictly maintained\056 Consequently\054 there is no evidence of sample\055to\055sample cross\055contamination or a shared laboratory vector\056\015 \015Based on the laboratory investigation\054 no assignable laboratory cause was identified involving the analyst\054 instrument\054 reagents\054 supplies\054 or monitored laboratory environment\056 Therefore\054 the likelihood of laboratory error contributing to this failure is considered minimal\054 and the original result is deemed valid\056)
>>
endobj
